<title>USA: TABLE - TEXAS UTILITIES SELLS $300 MLN DEBT.</title>
<headline>TABLE - TEXAS UTILITIES SELLS $300 MLN DEBT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue of unsecured debentures from Texas Utilities was priced on Wenesday, according to lead manager Morgan Stanley, Dean Witter &amp; Discover Co.</p>
<p>Texas Utilities is a utility holding company, that provides electric service in Dallas, Fort Worth, Midland, and other areas of Texas.</p>
<p>BORROWER TEXAS UTILITIES CO</p>
<p>AMT $300 MLN	 COUPON 7.17 PCT   MATURITY 8/1/2007</p>
<p>TYPE DEBENTURES    ISS PRICE 99.956  FIRST PAY DATE 2/1/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BAA2  YIELD 7.177 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB	 SPREAD +80 BPS    MAKE-WHOLE-CALL AT +10</p>
<p>						  BASIS POINTS OVER U.S.</p>
<p>							TREASURIES</p>
<p>((Caryn Trokie, U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678))</p>
</text>
